  "name": "Zombie Madness (SD2)",
  "category": "structure",
  "format": "classic",
  "manual": "Zombie toolbox control: chump, recur, and grind card advantage until a fat Zombie closes.\n\nCORE ENGINE — Pyramid Turtle (x3): let it die in battle, then Special Summon any Zombie with DEF 2000 or less from your Deck. Best fetch is Ryu Kokki (DEF 2000, 2400 ATK) — you trade a 1200 body for a 2400 beater that also blows up any Warrior/Spellcaster it battles. Other targets: Vampire Lord, Vampire Lady, Dark Dust Spirit, Double Coston, Regenerating Mummy, Soul-Absorbing Bone Tower.\n\nFREE BODIES — Call of the Mummy (x3): while you control no monsters, Special Summon 1 Zombie from your hand each turn for free. Turn-1 enabler; drop Ryu Kokki, Vampire Lord, or Despair from the Dark without tributing. Keep your field empty on their turn (bounce with Compulsory) so Call stays online.\n\nREANIMATION LOOP — Book of Life (x2): revive a Zombie from YOUR graveyard AND banish a monster from THEIRS — tempo plus graveyard disruption. Card of Safe Return turns every graveyard Special Summon (Book of Life, Vampire Lord's self-revive, Vampire Genesis) into a free draw, so land it early and chain summons.\n\nSTICKY BEATER — Vampire Lord (2000): on battle damage, mill a declared card type from their Deck; if an opponent's effect destroys it, it Special Summons itself back on your next Standby. Hard to kill for value.\n\nBOSS LINE — Vampire Genesis (3000): banish a Vampire Lord you control to Special Summon it, then once per turn discard a Zombie to revive a lower-Level Zombie from the GY — each revive also feeds Card of Safe Return. Double Coston counts as two tributes for a DARK monster, and Despair from the Dark (2800) is both discard fodder and a finisher that summons itself if the opponent mills it.\n\nTHEFT/DISRUPTION: Snatch Steal and Creature Swap take their best monster (Swap away a spent Pyramid Turtle after it has fetched). Backrow control is Torrential Tribute, Compulsory Evacuation Device (x3), Magic Jammer, and Dust Tornado; Reckless Greed draws 2 now; Heavy Storm / Giant Trunade / MST clear their backrow before you commit.\n\nWEAKNESSES: The deck lives in the graveyard — banishing, graveyard hate, and Nobleman-of-Crossout-style removal cripple Book of Life and the Vampire recursion. Call of the Mummy needs a truly empty field, and Card of Safe Return is a backrow liability that dies to their MST/Heavy Storm. No Extra Deck and a grindy clock mean faster combo decks can outrace you going second.",
  "sources": [
